ALSA: pcm: pass vendor (magic 'U') ioctls to the driver

NOT APPLIED. For bsp612/kernel (GKI 6.12.81), needed by drivers612/audio for the phone's closed
5.4-era audio HALs: the sound trigger HAL drives the ADSP listen sessions with SNDRV_LSM_* ioctls
and the voice HAL can issue SNDRV_VOICE_IOCTL_LCH, all with magic 'U', on the PCM fd. Samsung's 5.4
kernel passed them to the driver under CONFIG_AUDIO_QGKI (sound/core/pcm_native.c snd_user_ioctl,
pcm_compat.c snd_compressed_ioctl32 + snd_pcm_ops.compat_ioctl). GKI answers -ENOTTY, so voice wake-up
("Hi Bixby", "Hey Google") cannot work on 6.12 (drivers612/SPEC/02 rows AUD-50, AUD-35).

Native and compat callers both reach substream->ops->ioctl; the audio HAL process is 32-bit, the
techpack side (drivers612/audio/patches/audio-kernel/a52-lsm-compat-ioctl-gki.patch) tells them apart
with in_compat_syscall(). No exported symbol or structure changes: Module.symvers stays as it is.
Compile-checked out of tree (the patched pcm_native.c + pcm_compat.c built as a module object against
bsp612/out/lahaina). Never run. The kernel tree must keep its release string: mark both files
`git update-index --assume-unchanged` as done for the COMMAND_LINE_SIZE patch.

--- a/sound/core/pcm_native.c
+++ b/sound/core/pcm_native.c
@@ -3451,6 +3451,28 @@
 	return -ENOTTY;
 }
 
+/*
+ * a52sxq: ioctls with magic 'U' are the vendor commands of the 5.4-era Qualcomm audio HALs
+ * (sound trigger SNDRV_LSM_*, voice SNDRV_VOICE_IOCTL_LCH). The 5.4 QGKI kernel handed them to
+ * the driver (CONFIG_AUDIO_QGKI, snd_user_ioctl); the closed HALs still issue them on the PCM
+ * fd. Native and compat callers both land in substream->ops->ioctl; a driver that has 32-bit
+ * layouts tells them apart with in_compat_syscall().
+ */
+static int snd_pcm_vendor_ioctl(struct snd_pcm_substream *substream,
+				unsigned int cmd, void __user *arg)
+{
+	int res;
+
+	if (PCM_RUNTIME_CHECK(substream))
+		return -ENXIO;
+	if (!substream->ops || !substream->ops->ioctl)
+		return -ENOTTY;
+	res = snd_power_wait(substream->pcm->card);
+	if (res < 0)
+		return res;
+	return substream->ops->ioctl(substream, cmd, arg);
+}
+
 static long snd_pcm_ioctl(struct file *file, unsigned int cmd,
 			  unsigned long arg)
 {
@@ -3458,6 +3480,10 @@
 
 	pcm_file = file->private_data;
 
+	if (((cmd >> 8) & 0xff) == 'U')
+		return snd_pcm_vendor_ioctl(pcm_file->substream, cmd,
+					    (void __user *)arg);
+
 	if (((cmd >> 8) & 0xff) != 'A')
 		return -ENOTTY;
 
